{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J4jj3Pyjho4sWn8BHXzt4u","type":"tool_result","content":"812\t  \"_effort_level_comment\": \"PLAN-193 / ADR-149 Amendment 3 (dogfood: the shape of a new maintainer install, a decision of the authoring lane per A3.2 item 5; the Owner decisions S357 OQ-1, OQ-7 and OQ-8 cover adopters and new installs). Top-level effortLevel: in PROJECT settings it applies to every model the session uses and outranks a level a developer saved with /effort (Claude Code keeps those per model under modelSettings in user settings); a level set in .claude/settings.local.json outranks this file. Claude Opus 5.5 (the model pin above) runs at its default MEDIUM effort when no level is set, a default that an organization default effort replaces when the session runs the organization default model; Opus 5 and Fable 5 default to high. A maxEffortLevel caps any level, this one included. The key takes low, medium, high or xhigh; max is not one of its values, and Claude Code before 2.1.111 has no xhigh (this release needs 2.1.280, SUPPORT.md). New installs ship xhigh. On an existing install scripts/upgrade.sh writes xhigh only when you pass --adopt-setting effortLevel; when it moves the shipped pin claude-opus-5 to claude-opus-5-5 in a file that sets no level it writes high, the Opus 5 default; it never overwrites a value you set. Lower or delete the key to trade depth for cost and latency.\",\n813\t  \"effortLevel\": \"xhigh\",\n814\t  \"_deny_baseline_comment\": \"PLAN-153 Wave E item 3 — coarse harness-level deny baseline (docs/deny-baseline.md). Entries 5-24 of permissions.deny below mirror scripts/install.sh DENY_BASELINE_ENTRIES exactly: credential-store reads (~/.ssh, ~/.aws, npm/gcloud/kube/docker/git-credentials/netrc/pypirc), dotenv-family reads (SPECIFIC .env variants only — a deny rule cannot carry allow exceptions, so .env.example/.sample/.template stay readable by omission; unlisted variants like .env.secret pass this backstop), and the curl|bash tripwire. Honest limits: Read deny does not cover arbitrary subprocesses opening files, Bash(curl * | bash) is bypassable by rephrasing (that class is owned by check_bash_safety.py), and **/.env is cwd-anchored. Gate floor: check_harness_config.py DENY_BASELINE (4 entries — PLAN-161 C1 removed the three Write() twins: on current CLIs (>=2.1.216) Edit(X) deny rules cover ALL file-editing tools and Write(X) rules are unconsulted; the Owner accepted the old-CLI residual) must remain a subset of this list.\",\n815\t  \"_posture_comment\": \"PLAN-163 T5.3/OQ5(c) — Owner-ratified fail-closed session posture for the dogfood repo (CC 2.1.220 keys): permissions.defaultMode='manual' (2.1.2xx rename of the ask-first mode — every non-allowlisted tool call prompts). disableAutoMode was REMOVED 2026-08-03 (Owner decision, reversing the T5.3/OQ5(c) ratification): its observed effect is not only the documented 'no AUTOMATIC escalation mid-session' — it also strips 'auto' from the operator's native shift+tab mode cycle, i.e. the framework was removing a first-class Claude Code affordance from its own operator. Choosing the session permission mode is the operator's call, not the framework's. The fail-closed DEFAULT (defaultMode='manual') is unchanged: every session still STARTS ask-first; the operator can now cycle out of it deliberately, at the keyboard, for the session only. Measured 2026-08-03 with a neutralized user layer (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR): 'manual' prompts for Bash/Edit/Write; 'acceptEdits' does not. workflowSizeGuideline='medium' (advisory sizing guideline for Workflow-tool fan-outs; 2.1.220 binary schema: optional string enum ['unrestricted','small','medium','large'] — describe text: 'small' aims for fewer than 5 agents, 'medium' (the default) fewer than 15, 'large' fewer than 50, 'unrestricted' sends no guideline; a set value, including from managed settings, takes precedence over the /config toggle. Evidence: zod source at byte offset [REDACTED:rg] of the 2.1.220 binary, sha256 8addc857..., T2.2 extraction. 'medium' matches the current session guideline, ~15 agents), sandbox.network.strictAllowlist=true + sandbox.filesystem.disabled=false above. Templates carry the same keys COMMENTED (adopters opt in). The workflow-size text needs a re-read in the 2.1.295 binary before its numbers change; this settings edit records no new measurement. Rollback: to revert THIS change (the disableAutoMode removal), re-add the top-level key disableAutoMode with the value 'disable' — the string enum's sole legal value; a boolean makes 2.1.220 skip the WHOLE settings file (S286 live-fire). To roll back the remaining posture instead, remove defaultMode/workflowSizeGuideline + strictAllowlist in one commit — each key is independent and additive; no hook consumes them (harness-level only).\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"046a4659-3b58-4aa1-afb8-7e9a6b625253","uuid":"23157cb3-5396-4f26-a810-3b9c8f68e841","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:06:41.936Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/settings.json","content":"  \"_effort_level_comment\": \"PLAN-193 / ADR-149 Amendment 3 (dogfood: the shape of a new maintainer install, a decision of the authoring lane per A3.2 item 5; the Owner decisions S357 OQ-1, OQ-7 and OQ-8 cover adopters and new installs). Top-level effortLevel: in PROJECT settings it applies to every model the session uses and outranks a level a developer saved with /effort (Claude Code keeps those per model under modelSettings in user settings); a level set in .claude/settings.local.json outranks this file. Claude Opus 5.5 (the model pin above) runs at its default MEDIUM effort when no level is set, a default that an organization default effort replaces when the session runs the organization default model; Opus 5 and Fable 5 default to high. A maxEffortLevel caps any level, this one included. The key