{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F9S8MHDvnGJFmsFuWSkUs8","type":"tool_result","content":"363\tdef _sentinel_grants_path(sentinel_path: Path, target_rel: str) -> bool:\n364\t    \"\"\"Check whether a sentinel file grants the given target path.\n365\t\n366\t    PLAN-045 Wave 1 P0-01: verification is now two-tiered:\n367\t\n368\t    1. **Plaintext ``Approved-By:`` line** — existing fast check (visual\n369\t       Owner signoff marker).\n370\t    2. **Detached GPG signature** at ``<sentinel>.asc`` — verified\n371\t       against ``.claude/sentinel-signers.txt`` allowlist via\n372\t       ``_lib.gpg_verify.verify_detached``. Fail-CLOSED on: missing\n373\t       .asc, bad signature, signer fpr not in allowlist, empty\n374\t       allowlist.\n375\t\n376\t    **Environment bypass (interim, per ADR-010 amendment)**: setting\n377\t    ``CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK=<plan-id>`` + ``CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_ACK=I-ACCEPT``\n378\t    in the parent shell short-circuits the .asc requirement. This is a\n379\t    dual-auth mechanism mirroring the arbitration-kernel escape hatch;\n380\t    a sub-agent cannot forge the env vars. The override is logged via\n381\t    ``veto_triggered(reason_code=sentinel_unlock_used)``.\n382\t\n383\t    The sentinel must contain:\n384\t    1. A valid ``Approved-By: @<handle> <commit-sha>`` line\n385\t    2. A ``Scope:`` block listing the target path (one bullet per line)\n386\t    3. A sibling ``<sentinel>.asc`` detached GPG signature (unless env\n387\t       override is set)\n388\t    \"\"\"\n389\t    # PLAN-094 Wave C — session cache fast-path before expensive GPG verify.\n390\t    # Cache key (iter-1 P0 fix): (path, inode, mtime_ns, file_size, sha256_full,\n391\t    # target_rel, fmt_version). Cache value: granted (bool). env_override path\n392\t    # bypasses cache (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK semantic: must re-verify).\n393\t    global _SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS, _SENTINEL_CACHE_MISSES\n394\t\n395\t    # PLAN-045 Wave 1 P0-01: env-override (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK) detection.\n396\t    env = os.environ\n397\t    unlock_reason = (env.get(\"CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK\") or \"\").strip()\n398\t    unlock_ack = (env.get(\"CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_ACK\") or \"\").strip()\n399\t    env_override = bool(\n400\t        unlock_reason\n401\t        and unlock_ack == \"I-ACCEPT\"\n402\t        and re.match(r'^(ADR-\\d{3,4}|PLAN-\\d{3})-[a-z0-9-]{3,100}$', unlock_reason)  # PLAN-086 Wave I.1 — ADR-119 tightening\n403\t    )\n404\t\n405\t    # PLAN162_FIX_1 — SIGNATURE RAIL FIRST, and it is target-FREE.\n406\t    #\n407\t    # Two reasons the order changed (both are the fix):\n408\t    #   * #1 — verifying once per SENTINEL instead of once per\n409\t    #     (sentinel x target) is the whole amplification collapse; and\n410\t    #   * #10 — the target-keyed grant cache below hashes only\n411\t    #     approved.md, so a mutated .asc / allowlist / registry would ride\n412\t    #     a stale True if the grant fast-path ran first. Consulting the\n413\t    #     material-keyed rail up front makes a revocation land immediately.\n414\t    _trusted_text = None  # type: Optional[str]\n415\t    if not env_override:\n416\t        if not _signature_rail_ok(sentinel_path):\n417\t            return False\n418\t    else:\n419\t        # PLAN162_FIX_S2 — inside an unlock window the GPG rail is skipped\n420\t        # entirely, so the only thing separating an Owner-signed sentinel\n421\t        # from one the AGENT just wrote is provenance. See the module note\n422\t        # above for the two proof forms and the residual.\n423\t        _authorized, _trusted_text = _unlock_trusted_text(sentinel_path, env=env)\n424\t        if not _authorized:\n425\t            return False\n426\t\n427\t    # PLAN-094 Wave C — session cache fast-path (now scope-only).\n428\t    # Cache key (iter-1 P0 fix): (path, inode, mtime_ns, file_size, sha256_full,\n429\t    # target_rel, fmt_version). Cache value: granted (bool). env_override path\n430\t    # bypasses cache (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK semantic: must re-verify).\n431\t    _cache_key = None\n432\t    if not _sentinel_cache_disabled() and not env_override:\n433\t        _cache_key = _compute_sentinel_cache_key(sentinel_path, target_rel)\n434\t        if _cache_key is not None:\n435\t            _cached = _SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE.get(_cache_key)\n436\t            if _cached is not None:\n437\t                _SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS += 1\n438\t                return _cached\n439\t            _SENTINEL_CACHE_MISSES += 1\n440\t\n441\t    # PLAN162_FIX_S2R2 (codex P1-1): under an unlock window the bytes that\n442\t    # decide are the ANCHORED bytes, never whatever an in-window writer"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"046a4659-3b58-4aa1-afb8-7e9a6b625253","uuid":"004d66da-7876-4915-a082-93a9ae27d5a2","timestamp":"2026-11-13T18:08:12.248Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/sentinels.py","content":"def _sentinel_grants_path(sentinel_path: Path, target_rel: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check whether a sentinel file grants the given target path.\n\n    PLAN-045 Wave 1 P0-01: verification is now two-tiered:\n\n    1. **Plaintext ``Approved-By:`` line** — existing fast check (visual\n       Owner signoff marker).\n    2. **Detached GPG signature** at ``<sentinel>.asc`` — verified\n       against ``.claude/sentinel-signers.txt`` allowlist via\n       ``_lib.gpg_verify.verify_detached``. Fail-CLOSED on: missing\n       .asc, bad signature, signer fpr not in allowlist, empty\n       allowlist.\n\n    **Environment bypass (interim, per ADR-010 amendment)**: setting\n    ``CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK=<plan-id>`` + ``CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_ACK=I-ACCEPT``\n    in the parent shell short-circuits the .asc requirement. This is a\n    dual-auth mechanism mirroring the arbitration-kernel escape hatch;\n    a sub-agent cannot forge the env vars. The override is logged via\n    ``veto_triggered(reason_code=sentinel_unlock_used)``.\n\n    The sentinel must contain:\n    1. A valid ``Approved-By: @<handle> <commit-sha>`` line\n    2. A ``Scope:`` block listing the target path (one bullet per line)\n    3. A sibling ``<sentinel>.asc`` detached GPG signature (unless env\n       override is set)\n    \"\"\"\n    # PLAN-094 Wave C — session cache fast-path before expensive GPG verify.\n    # Cache key (iter-1 P0 fix): (path, inode, mtime_ns, file_size, sha256_full,\n    # target_rel, fmt_version). Cache value: granted (bool). env_override path\n    # bypasses cache (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK semantic: must re-verify).\n    global _SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS, _SENTINEL_CACHE_MISSES\n\n    # PLAN-045 Wave 1 P0-01: env-override (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK) detection.\n    env = os.environ\n    unlock_reason = (env.get(\"CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK\") or \"\").strip()\n    unlock_ack = (env.get(\"CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK_ACK\") or \"\").strip()\n    env_override = bool(\n        unlock_reason\n        and unlock_ack == \"I-ACCEPT\"\n        and re.match(r'^(ADR-\\d{3,4}|PLAN-\\d{3})-[a-z0-9-]{3,100}$', unlock_reason)  # PLAN-086 Wave I.1 — ADR-119 tightening\n    )\n\n    # PLAN162_FIX_1 — SIGNATURE RAIL FIRST, and it is target-FREE.\n    #\n    # Two reasons the order changed (both are the fix):\n    #   * #1 — verifying once per SENTINEL instead of once per\n    #     (sentinel x target) is the whole amplification collapse; and\n    #   * #10 — the target-keyed grant cache below hashes only\n    #     approved.md, so a mutated .asc / allowlist / registry would ride\n    #     a stale True if the grant fast-path ran first. Consulting the\n    #     material-keyed rail up front makes a revocation land immediately.\n    _trusted_text = None  # type: Optional[str]\n    if not env_override:\n        if not _signature_rail_ok(sentinel_path):\n            return False\n    else:\n        # PLAN162_FIX_S2 — inside an unlock window the GPG rail is skipped\n        # entirely, so the only thing separating an Owner-signed sentinel\n        # from one the AGENT just wrote is provenance. See the module note\n        # above for the two proof forms and the residual.\n        _authorized, _trusted_text = _unlock_trusted_text(sentinel_path, env=env)\n        if not _authorized:\n            return False\n\n    # PLAN-094 Wave C — session cache fast-path (now scope-only).\n    # Cache key (iter-1 P0 fix): (path, inode, mtime_ns, file_size, sha256_full,\n    # target_rel, fmt_version). Cache value: granted (bool). env_override path\n    # bypasses cache (CEO_SENTINEL_UNLOCK semantic: must re-verify).\n    _cache_key = None\n    if not _sentinel_cache_disabled() and not env_override:\n        _cache_key = _compute_sentinel_cache_key(sentinel_path, target_rel)\n        if _cache_key is not None:\n            _cached = _SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE.get(_cache_key)\n            if _cached is not None:\n                _SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS += 1\n                return _cached\n            _SENTINEL_CACHE_MISSES += 1\n\n    # PLAN162_FIX_S2R2 (codex P1-1): under an unlock window the bytes that\n    # decide are the ANCHORED bytes, never whatever an in-window writer","numLines":80,"startLine":363,"totalLines":582}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F9S8MHDvnGJFmsFuWSkUs8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
