or) falls back to allow-all (line 639).\n  (b) If only guards.py fails to import, the first try at lines 118-127 silently sets _CANONICAL_GUARDS = [] with no stderr line. The package __init__ does not import guards, so bind still succeeds and _COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR stays None. Every path then classifies as non-canonical. That silently opens: the Edit gate, the Bash canonical-write matcher (posture_tables.py:53,160), bash_indirect_guard.py:410, the check_codex_filewrite DENY_LIST and the --is-canonical oracle. mcp__ events then crash on a NameError for _MCP_WRITE_PATH_KEYS, which fails open. Kernel hard-deny still covers the kernel paths.\n- Failure scenario: an adopter's upgrade is interrupted, or _lib is pruned by hand, so check_canonical_edit.py is present but a _lib/canonical_edit/*.py file is not. Every file edit in every session is then blocked with \"canonical_edit integrity failure\" until the adopter reinstalls. It is recoverable through Bash, but it is the \"blocking a legitimate session\" class.\n- Minimal fix:\n  1. In the fallback main(), parse stdin and block only when a candidate path's lower-cased first segment is in _CANONICAL_PREFIXES_FOLDED; allow everything else.\n  2. Move the guards import into the same integrity try, so a guards-only failure sets _COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR and is not silent.\n  3. Or, at minimum, declare the block-all posture in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] (hooks split, plus Known-open) and correct the docstring.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\n1. .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325. _sentinel_patterns() walks the AST of check_canonical_edit.py looking for `_PATTERNS`, which moved with _find_sentinels to _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py:238-249.\n   - Effect: the boot check sentinels_pending_gpg now always runs on the 4-pattern fallback and prints \"[padrões em FALLBACK — a autoridade não foi lida]\".\n   - It no longer reports pending sentinels under architect/wave-0a, wave-0b, wave-1-2, wave-minus-1, staging/review or audit-v2/architect/round-*.\n   - The S321 comment (\"os padrões são EXTRAÍDOS por AST do arquivo que os define\") is no longer true, and no test covers derived=True.\n   - Fix: parse paths.py.\n2. .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceremony_toolkit/preflight.py:50-62. _canonical_patterns() requires a top-level `_CANONICAL_GUARDS = [...]` in check_canonical_edit.py. The only remaining assignment sits inside an except block (line 124, an empty list).\n   - Effect: the default path of collect_modified_canonical_paths / validate_sentinel_pack always returns canonical_guard_policy_unavailable. That fails closed and only affects maintainers.\n   - Every test passes canonical_patterns explicitly, so this path is untested.\n   - Fix: read _lib/canonical_edit/guards.py.\n3. check_canonical_edit.py has stale or dead text:\n   - The docstring at lines 36-40 states a fail-open contract the facade no longer has.\n   - Lines 125-127 define _SKILL_CONTENT_RE, _SKILL_LOADED_RE and _VALID_BLOCKED_TOOLS, which nothing in the hook uses.\n   - The comment at lines 165-168 ends in a dangling fragment.\n   - The fallback main prints a raw Claude-shaped decision, which a Codex-host wire would not honor. The hook's own entry.py:16-18 calls that a silent fail-open.\n4. .claude/hooks/check_cost_envelope.py:187.\n   - The project string is now abspath(CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR) instead of the raw value, and the composite spend key hashes it (_lib/cost_envelope.py:132-139). A CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR with a trailing slash or ./.. segments starts a fresh daily, 7-day and 30-day ledger after upgrade: spend recorded under the old key no longer counts against the cap.\n   - An import failure of _lib.runtime_paths also silently disables the envelope, which the CHANGELOG line (\"without an absolute CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\") does not mention.\n   - Low impact; declare it, or keep the key derivation byte-compatible.\n\ncheck_harness_config.py: no defect found beyond the above.","decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","sentence":"No declared condition this payload touches is false and I found no P0, but one undeclared P1 should be declared in CHANGELOG [1.4.4] or fixed before GA: when a component fails to import, the canonical-edit fallback blocks every edit, canonical or not, and a guards-only import failure silently disables the gate."}}}
